   "**A pause granted by Washington and ended by Kyiv is a lesson about who owns the war** — the refinery campaign was suspended for an American election calendar, not for a military reason; the direct effect is a refinery on the Volga burning two weeks later; the compound consequence is that the one lever the White House held over Ukrainian targeting has been shown to expire, and any future request for restraint will be read in Kyiv as a request to absorb strikes like Thursday's while the other side refuels",
