  "cause": "**Binance, the world's largest cryptocurrency exchange, said $6.3 billion of funds have been impacted** in what the industry is calling the biggest crypto theft on record. The exchange said it had \"worked with blockchain partners to freeze affected assets, with around **$3 billion frozen on-chain so far**\", **temporarily suspended all deposits and withdrawals**, and would cover all losses — \"user funds are safe\" (Straits Times/Bloomberg, NYT). **Blockchain intelligence firm TRM Labs attributed the attack to TraderTraitor, North Korea's elite hacking unit, \"based on robust on- and off-chain intelligence… with high confidence\"**, calling it \"the largest crypto theft on record\"; the previous record was **Bybit in February 2025, at almost $1.5 billion** (Straits Times). **Tether froze more than $1.5 billion** of its stablecoin \"related to a potential Binance exchange hack\"; **Circle froze $800 million**; **Bitcoin fell 3% in the US session and a further 3% in Asia, below $77,000**, its lowest since September, with other tokens selling off. The same day, **Polymarket halted trading for an hour** after a third-party software provider was compromised. Binance's emergency backstop, the **Secure Asset Fund for Users, is normally maintained at around $1 billion** — against $6.3 billion impacted, in a sector already carrying recent losses at **Bitget** and through **tampered Ledger devices** (Straits Times).",
