   "**The hinge is whether custody, reserves and freezing become disclosed instruments rather than press statements** — the moment exchanges publish proof-of-reserves continuously and under independent attestation rather than quarterly in a blog post; the moment reserve funds are sized to the assets they hold; the moment stablecoin issuers must publish the standard by which they freeze a wallet and the appeal route against it; and the moment the \"regulatory clarity\" being promised specifies custody liability rather than only token classification — the chain can be broken. §19:20 makes the causal point this story keeps proving: thoughts and feelings are not free of account, and among the things that must be accounted for are \"robbery and thieving\", \"giving false testimony\" and \"stinginess\"."
