   "**The hinge is whether the FDLR and M23 files are adjudicated in one mechanism with dates** — the moment the Accords acquire a joint verification body publishing findings on both armed groups, with both capitals accepting its findings in advance; the moment mineral exports carry a certified chain of custody that a smelter in Asia cannot bypass; the moment the banking restrictions are paired with a monitored route back into the dollar system on compliance milestones rather than being lifted as a favour; and the moment M23's absorption into the Kabila-led FRN coalition is treated as a political process requiring a political answer rather than a military one — the chain can be broken. §4:185 does not take sides; it names plunder, deception and killing in wars as the same contradiction of the teaching, whoever commits them."
