  "verse": "It contradicts the truth of the laws and recommendations of the wellspring of all existence and therefore of the true teaching of the prophets if you do unright, if you steal and rob, if you plunder and lie and deceive, if you slander and calumniate, if you practise amongst yourselves acts of Gewalt or other Gewalt and killing as a punishment and in battles or anywhere else.",
  "verseSrc": "Chapter 4, Verse 185",
  "hinge": "The cause is not the sanction and it is not M23. It is the choice — by Kigali, whether the army's presence in the eastern Congo is a security requirement to be negotiated or an occupation to be maintained; by Kinshasa, whether the FDLR is disarmed or used; by Washington, whether the Accords acquire a verification mechanism with published findings on both parties instead of a designation list; by the refiners and smelters, whether uncertified coltan and gold have a market at all; and by the leagues and sponsors, whether a reputation built on sport survives being asked the question in writing. §4:185 locates the contradiction not in one side's account but in the deeds themselves — plunder, deception, and killing in battles. A peace accord signed in December under which both parties are still fighting is that contradiction with a signature on it."
